; M1e S1e.2.1 — `(absent)` with nothing to be absent.
;
; The sibling `empty_absent.ein` is `(absent ?x)`, whose sub-plan compiles to
; no steps and which has had a *CompileError* naming that exact hazard since
; S1.22.0 — "the guard would fail against every KB and its candidates would be
; retired permanently". With no argument at all the same thing happened and
; nothing said so: `absent` fell through to the ordinary relation path, matched
; the empty extent of a relation nobody declared, and retired the rule for the
; run in silence.
;
; So the two files are one hazard at two arities, and only one of them was
; refused.
(relation p T)
(relation q T)

(rule guard-of-nothing ()
  :match  (and (p ?x) (absent))
  :assert (q ?x))
